[
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we have the following result: <code>ContinuousOn (CFC.sqrt) {S : Matrix ι ι ℝ | 0 ≤ S}</code>? (I care about square real matrices here but I don't mind more generality <span aria-label=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f601\" role=\"img\" title=\"grinning face with smiling eyes\">:grinning_face_with_smiling_eyes:</span>)</p>",
        "id": 600698185,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780670147
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CFC.continuousOn_sqrt#doc\">docs#CFC.continuousOn_sqrt</a> ?</p>",
        "id": 600698412,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780670198
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks a lot! I apologize, <code>exact?</code> did not find it <span aria-label=\"sad\" class=\"emoji emoji-2639\" role=\"img\" title=\"sad\">:sad:</span></p>",
        "id": 600698641,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780670258
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"thinking\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f914\" role=\"img\" title=\"thinking\">:thinking:</span> maybe we don't have the <code>Isometric</code> instance for <code>Matrix n n ℝ</code> (and in any case you would need a local instance even for <code>Matrix n n ℂ</code>).</p>",
        "id": 600698649,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780670259
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The problem you're suffering from fundamentally is that we don't have any definition of real C⋆-algebras (and therefore also no theorems about them).</p>",
        "id": 600699492,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780670458
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It seems that <code>NonUnitalNormedRing (Matrix n n ℝ)</code> is lacking as well.</p>",
        "id": 600699572,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780670486
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>right, that's what I mean about a local instance. We have no norm on matrices by default.</p>",
        "id": 600699654,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780670510
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh ok I see. First time working with matrices, I'll try some things then</p>",
        "id": 600699849,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780670560
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If you <code>open scoped Matrix.Norms.L2Operator</code>, then you'll get the <code>CStarRing</code> instance. With that scope, you'll have access to <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.l2_opNorm_diagonal#doc\">docs#Matrix.l2_opNorm_diagonal</a>. You can use this with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.IsHermitian.cfc_eq#doc\">docs#Matrix.IsHermitian.cfc_eq</a> (or maybe <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Matrix.IsHermitian.cfcHom_eq_cfcAux#doc\">docs#Matrix.IsHermitian.cfcHom_eq_cfcAux</a>) to establish the <code>IsometricContinuousFunctionalCalculus</code> instance you need.</p>",
        "id": 600700500,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780670738
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok thanks a lot, I'll see what I can do with that!</p>",
        "id": 600701000,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780670867
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>When you prove this instance, please PR it and ping me.</p>",
        "id": 600701256,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780670930
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok! I'll share the code here as well</p>",
        "id": 600701366,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780670955
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm struggling with <code>TopologicalSpace</code> instances. When using <code>Matrix.IsHermitian.cfcHom_eq_cfcAux</code>, the topological space is the one coming from <code>instTopologicalSpaceMatrix</code> whereas in the <code>cfcHom</code> of the proof, it is the one derived from the norm (I think).</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">scoped</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MatrixOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Norms</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">L2Operator</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Fintype</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CStarRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferInstance</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsometricContinuousFunctionalCalculus</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsSelfAdjoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">predicate_zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">spectrum_nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousFunctionalCalculus</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">spectrum_nonempty</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exists_cfc_of_predicate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">isometric</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsHermitian</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isHermitian_iff_isSelfAdjoint</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA'</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isSelfAdjoint</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">this</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Matrix</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsHermitian</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cfcHom_eq_cfcAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hA'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- fails</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 600706505,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780672312
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>That shouldn't be the case, the norm instance should make the topology it induces defeq, see <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/9f6a6b1d07396a49fa4c3a4744522208518dafa8/Mathlib/Analysis/CStarAlgebra/Matrix.lean#L155-L170\">here</a></p>",
        "id": 600708528,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780672870
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But indeed, they are not defeq at the correct transparency level.</p>",
        "id": 600709474,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780673134
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I can look into fixing this later, but it will have to wait until next week. For now, you can just add</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">backward</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isDefEq</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">respectTransparency</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">false</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>prior to your <code>instance</code></p>",
        "id": 600709674,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1780673201
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks a lot for your help, I'll work on that and post any updates here</p>",
        "id": 600710183,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1780673338
    },
